---
name: "Home"
title: "Lightening Lives | Genetic testing that reaches every community"
description: "Genetic and molecular diagnostics from a dried blood spot: REASSURED tests that screen and confirm inherited disorders in one test. ICMR approved."
film: true
socialAlt: "One test to screen. The same test to confirm. A map of India made of dried blood spot cards, with Delhi, Maharashtra, Jharkhand, Telangana and Tamil Nadu named."
---
{#- The home page (content/website-content.md 5.1, cut to nine sections by the marketing review of 25
    October 2026): the film; who works with us; Innovate (the gel), Diagnose (the comparison), REASSURED,
    Transform lives (the testing model); one platform; the need and our work; three ways to partner.
    The film's markup is unchanged; the film itself is src/js/site/scene.js. -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' -%}
{%- from "picture.njk" import picture with context %}
{%- from "map.njk" import mapSection with context %}
{%- from "doors.njk" import doorList with context %}
{%- from "model.njk" import testingModel %}
{%- from "credentials.njk" import credentials %}

  <!-- The opening: an announcement when there is one, the heading, and the film beside it, which
       comes to rest on a map with every state we work in pinned; the partners slide along its foot -->
  <section class="hero" id="top" data-film data-film-state="playing" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div class="hero-veil"></div>
    <div class="hero-frame" data-frame></div>

    <div class="hero-text" data-hero-text>
      {%- set news = announcements.items | upcoming %}
      {%- if news.length %}
      <ul class="hero-news rise" style="--i:0" aria-label="Announcements" data-news>
        {%- for item in news %}
        <li data-start="{{ item.start }}" data-end="{{ item.end }}"{% if item.preview %} data-preview{% endif %}{% if not item.live or (loop.index0 > 0) %} hidden{% endif %}>
          {%- set when = item.when.split(" ") %}
          <a class="news" href="{{ item.link.href }}"><span class="news-stub" aria-hidden="true">{% if when.length == 2 and r/^\d/.test(when[0]) %}<span class="news-month news-label">{{ when[1].slice(0, 3) }}</span><span class="news-day">{{ when[0] }}</span>{% else %}{% icon "calendar-days" %}{% endif %}</span><span class="news-body"><span class="news-text"><span class="news-tag">{{ item.tag or "Event" }}</span> <strong>{{ item.text }}</strong><span class="sr-only">, {{ item.when }}</span></span><span class="news-cta">{{ item.link.text }}{% icon "arrow-right" %}</span></span></a>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- endif %}
      <h1 id="hero-h" class="display rise" style="--i:1">Genetic testing that <span class="h-mark">reaches every community.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead lead rise" style="--i:2">Genetic and molecular diagnostics from a dried blood spot: one test to screen and confirm, patient, carrier or unaffected, built to the <a class="lead-link" href="#reassured">REASSURED</a> standard.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions rise" style="--i:3">
        <a class="btn btn-solid" {{ {} | enquire | safe }}>{{ site.cta.text }}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-line" href="/technology/">How the test works</a>
      </div>
      {{ credentials([
        { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" },
        { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" },
        { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
      ], "hero-note rise", "--i:4") }}
    </div>

    <!-- After the text in the page, so the keyboard reaches the buttons first; placed beside it by the stylesheet -->
    <div class="film-screen" data-film-screen>
      <img class="film-poster" src="/assets/img/site-drop.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="A dried blood spot card held open, with a drop of blood falling towards its dashed collection circle. Rows of closed cards fade into the distance behind it." decoding="async">
      <div class="places-wrap" data-places-wrap inert>
        <h2 class="sr-only" id="places-h">Where we work: {{ work.film.length }} states</h2>
        <ol class="places" data-places>
          {%- for place in work.film %}
          <li data-place="{{ place.id }}"><button type="button" class="place-pin" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="place-card" aria-label="{{ place.name }}"><img class="place-emblem" src="/assets/logo/lightening-lives-emblem.svg" alt="" width="60" height="60"></button><b aria-hidden="true">{{ place.name }}</b></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
        <div class="place-card" id="place-card" aria-live="polite" hidden>
          <p class="place-card-h" id="place-card-h" data-place-name></p>
          <p class="place-card-line" data-place-line></p>
          <a class="link place-card-link" href="#map" data-place-link>See on the map
            {{ arrow | safe }}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-solid film-play" data-film-play hidden>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" width="14" height="16" viewBox="0 0 14 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M1 1.2v13.6a.6.6 0 0 0 .92.5l10.7-6.8a.6.6 0 0 0 0-1L1.92.7A.6.6 0 0 0 1 1.2Z"/></svg>
        Play the film
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Who works with us, along the foot of the opening: a row of cells whose logos change in place, a
         few at a time (main.js, initLogos); every name is in the list a screen reader hears -->
    <div class="hero-foot" id="partners" data-logos>
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="partners-h">We work with</h2>
      {%- set shown = partners.logos | selectattr("published") %}
      <div class="logo-cycle" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="partners-h" aria-describedby="partners-note">
        <p class="sr-only" id="partners-note">The logos change every few seconds. Press Enter to stop or start them.</p>
        <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" data-logo-status></p>
        <ul class="sr-only">
          {%- for p in shown %}
          <li>{{ p.name }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <ul class="logo-cells" aria-hidden="true" data-logo-pool='[{%- for p in shown %}{"src":"/assets/logo/partners/{{ p.file }}","w":{{ p.width }},"h":{{ p.height }},"ratio":{{ (p.width / p.height) | round(3) }}}{{ "," if not loop.last }}{%- endfor %}]'>
          {%- for p in shown %}{% if loop.index0 < 6 %}
          <li class="logo-cell"><img src="/assets/logo/partners/{{ p.file }}" width="{{ p.width }}" height="{{ p.height }}" alt="" style="--ratio: {{ (p.width / p.height) | round(3) }}" decoding="async"></li>
          {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Innovate: the invention in one picture, the gel read-out -->
  <section id="innovate" class="section" aria-labelledby="innovate-h">
    <div class="wrap split-gel">
      <div class="split-words">
        <h2 id="innovate-h" class="h2"><span class="h-mark">Innovate.</span> Patient, carrier or unaffected, read in one run.</h2>
        <p class="lead mt-5">Mutation-specific PCR, read on an agarose gel, separates the three in a single test. Screening and confirmation happen together, from a dried blood spot.</p>
        <ul class="ticks mt-7">
          <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<p><strong>Screening cum confirmatory.</strong> No second test and no second visit.</p></li>
          <li>{% icon "baby" %}<p><strong>From birth.</strong> Newborns can be tested at birth.</p></li>
          <li>{% icon "thermometer" %}<p><strong>No cold chain.</strong> Dried cards travel at room temperature.</p></li>
          <li>{% icon "flask-conical" %}<p><strong>No DNA extraction.</strong> A punch from the card goes straight into the reaction.</p></li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link mt-7" href="/technology/">How the test works
          {{ arrow | safe }}
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="gel" data-gel>
        {#- The gel, flat (26 October 2026: the user found the 3D one did not serve the purpose): the
            poster's read-out drawn in HTML and CSS. The three samples are the subject; the marker and
            the control are the references they are read against, set quieter. -#}
        <div class="gel-slab" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a LitLife™ gel, after our conference poster: a size marker, then a patient, an unaffected sample and a carrier, each with its own pattern of bands, and an empty no-DNA control.">
          {%- set lanes = [
            { name: "Marker", kind: "marker", bands: [17.7, 24.6, 30, 35.8, 42.5, 48.3, 54.2, 61.3, 67.3, 73.8, 80.6, 94.2], heavy: [42.5, 67.3] },
            { name: "Patient", bands: [48.5, 80] },
            { name: "Unaffected", bands: [48.5, 65] },
            { name: "Carrier", bands: [48.5, 65, 80] },
            { name: "Control", kind: "control", note: "No DNA", bands: [] }
          ] %}
          {%- for lane in lanes %}
          <div class="lane{% if lane.kind %} lane-{{ lane.kind }}{% endif %}">
            <span class="lane-name"><b>{{ lane.name }}</b></span>
            <div class="lane-track"><span class="lane-well"></span>{% for y in lane.bands %}<span class="lane-band{% if lane.heavy and y in lane.heavy %} is-heavy{% endif %}" style="--y: {{ y }}%"></span>{% endfor %}{% if lane.note %}<span class="lane-note" aria-hidden="true">{{ lane.note }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
          </div>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        {#- The read-out, from the content file (5.1, Innovate: one band lower, patient; one upper,
            unaffected; both, carrier), named by where the bands stand on the gel as drawn, under the
            top band that every sample shows. Each one lights its lane, pointed at, focused or chosen. -#}
        <ul class="gel-key">
          {%- for key in [
            { lane: 1, name: "Patient", read: "Bottom band", glyph: "lower" },
            { lane: 2, name: "Unaffected", read: "Middle band", glyph: "upper" },
            { lane: 3, name: "Carrier", read: "Middle and bottom", glyph: "both" }
          ] %}
          <li><button type="button" class="gel-key-btn" data-gel-lane="{{ key.lane }}" aria-pressed="false"><span class="gel-glyph is-{{ key.glyph }}" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="gel-key-text"><strong>{{ key.name }}</strong><span>{{ key.read }}</span></span></button></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <figcaption>How a LitLife™ gel reads, after our conference poster: every sample shows the top band; under it, a patient, an unaffected person and a carrier each show their own pattern, read against a size marker, in one run. The control, with no DNA, stays empty.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Diagnose: the problem and the proof in one place (the poster's comparison) -->
  <section id="diagnose" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="diagnose-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="diagnose-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7"><span class="h-mark">Diagnose.</span> What changes when you switch.</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Today, screening and confirmation are two tests and two visits, and liquid blood needs a cold chain. Many people screened are never confirmed.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="compare-table compare-compact mt-12" aria-labelledby="diagnose-h">
        <caption>From our presentation to the haematology community, October 2026.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            <th scope="col">Conventional screening tests</th>
            <th scope="col">Conventional confirmatory tests</th>
            <th scope="col" class="is-ours">LitLife™</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- set compared = [
            ["Sample", "20 to 50 µl of blood", "1 to 2 ml of EDTA blood", "A spot of blood on a card"],
            ["Storage and transport", "Cold chain", "Cold chain", "Room temperature"],
            ["Pre-processing", "Yes", "Yes", "None"],
            ["A second test to confirm", "Yes", "No", "No"],
            ["Newborns", "No", "After 72 hours of birth", "At birth"],
            ["Throughput", "Low", "Low", "High"]
          ] %}
          {%- for row in compared %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ row[0] }}</th>
            <td data-label="Screening">{{ row[1] }}</td>
            <td data-label="Confirmation">{{ row[2] }}</td>
            <td data-label="LitLife™" class="is-ours">{{ row[3] }}</td>
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. REASSURED, as the client likes it, in the poster's words -->
  {% include "reassured.njk" %}

  <!-- 6. Transform lives: the poster's testing model -->
  <section id="model" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="model-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="model-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7"><span class="h-mark">Transform lives.</span> Six steps, from a finger prick to a family in care.</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">A test only matters if its result reaches care. Our testing model follows each sample all the way, with counselling and support for every family.</p>
      </div>
      {{ testingModel("mt-12") }}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7. One platform: what we test for, and the open place for the next condition -->
  <section id="tests" class="section" aria-labelledby="tests-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="tests-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">One platform. <span class="h-mark">Built for any inherited condition.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">The LitLife™ method adapts to new mutations. So far it reads inherited blood and muscle disorders, with coagulation and pharmacogenomics next.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="platform mt-12">
        {%- set families = [
          { icon: "droplets", name: "Blood disorders", sub: "Haemoglobinopathies", href: "/solutions/#haemoglobinopathies", tests: [
            { name: "Sickle cell anaemia", code: "LitLife™-SCA", href: "/solutions/sickle-cell-anaemia/" },
            { name: "Sickle-beta thalassaemia", code: "LitLife™-SiBThal217", href: "/solutions/sickle-cell-anaemia/" },
            { name: "Beta thalassaemia", code: "LitLife™-BThal", href: "/solutions/thalassaemia/" },
            { name: "Alpha thalassaemia", code: "LitLife™-AlphaThal", href: "/solutions/thalassaemia/" },
            { name: "HbD and HbE", code: "Also available", href: "/solutions/thalassaemia/" }
          ] },
          { icon: "activity", name: "Muscle disorders", sub: "Musculopathies", href: "/solutions/#musculopathies", tests: [
            { name: "Spinal muscular atrophy", code: "LitLife™-SMA", href: "/solutions/spinal-muscular-atrophy/" },
            { name: "Duchenne muscular dystrophy", code: "Talk to us", href: "/solutions/#dmd" },
            { name: "Limb-girdle muscular dystrophy", code: "Talk to us", href: "/solutions/#lgmd" }
          ] }
        ] %}
        {%- for family in families %}
        <div class="family">
          <div class="family-head"><span class="icon-tile">{% icon family.icon %}</span><div><h3 class="h3">{{ family.name }}</h3><p class="family-sub">{{ family.sub }}</p></div></div>
          <ul class="family-list">
            {%- for test in family.tests %}
            <li><a href="{{ test.href }}"><span>{{ test.name }}</span><span class="family-code">{{ test.code }}</span>{% icon "arrow-right" %}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
        <div class="family-next">
          <p class="family-dev">{% icon "flask-conical" %}<span><strong>In development:</strong> a blood coagulation panel and pharmacogenomics.</span></p>
          <a class="next-tile" href="/solutions/#develop">
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "plus" %}</span>
            <span><strong>Your condition next.</strong> We develop and validate a test when a programme needs one.</span>
            {% icon "arrow-right" %}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8. The need and our work, with the latest work beneath the map -->
  {%- call mapSection({ h2: 'Where the need is, <span class="h-mark">and where we work</span>' }) %}
      <div class="work-row">
        <h3 class="work-row-h">Our latest work</h3>
        <ul class="work-cards">
          <li class="work-card">
            <a href="/our-work/#sites">
              <span class="work-pic">{{ picture("place-nandurbar", "A monsoon-green gorge in Maharashtra.", "(min-width: 64rem) 24rem, 90vw", { position: "62% 50%" }) }}</span>
              <span class="work-kind">Field programmes</span>
              <span class="work-title">Population and newborn screening in nine states and Delhi</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="work-card">
            <a href="/our-work/">
              <span class="work-pic">{{ picture("work-poster-v9", "The top of the company's conference poster on screening and confirming sickle cell anaemia and other haemoglobinopathies in one test.", "(min-width: 64rem) 24rem, 90vw", { position: "50% 0%" }) }}</span>
              <span class="work-kind">Conference poster</span>
              <span class="work-title">One test to screen and confirm sickle cell anaemia, presented to haematologists</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li class="work-card work-card-plain">
            <a href="/technology/#patents">
              <span class="work-pic work-pic-icon work-pic-patents" aria-hidden="true"><span class="patent-seal">{% icon "award" %}</span><span class="patent-flags"><span>IN</span><span>JP</span><span>{% icon "globe" %}</span></span></span>
              <span class="work-kind">Patents</span>
              <span class="work-title">Patents granted in India and Japan, and published internationally</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link mt-6" href="/our-work/">All our work
          {{ arrow | safe }}
        </a>
      </div>
  {%- endcall %}

  <!-- 9. Three ways to partner, signed by the founder -->
  <section id="contact" class="section closing-home" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="contact-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Partner with us. <span class="h-mark">Tell us what you need to test for.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Laboratories, health programmes and funders work with us to bring confirmed genetic diagnosis to the people who need it.</p>
      </div>
      {{ doorList(false, "mt-12") }}
      <div class="signed">
        {{ picture("person-founders", "Dr. Giriraj Ratan Chandak and Mrs. Nidhi Chandak", "5rem", { class: "signed-pic" }) }}
        <p><strong>Dr. Giriraj Ratan Chandak</strong>, MD, PhD, DNB. Founder and CEO; formerly Chief Scientist at CSIR-CCMB and Director of CDFD. <a class="link" href="/about/">About us {{ arrow | safe }}</a></p>
        <p class="signed-reach"><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{% icon "mail" %}{{ site.email }}</a><a href="tel:{{ site.tel }}">{% icon "phone" %}{{ site.phone | replace(" ", "&nbsp;") | safe }}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
